The three primes named in Sec. 6.7 are 17, 281, 349.
  17: split, in the 508-prime scan, reproduced here
  281: split, in the 508-prime scan, not reproduced here
  349: split, in the 508-prime scan, not reproduced here
  reproduced here : [17]
  not reproduced  : [281, 349]

READING.  A reconstruction whose residual error saturates the working
precision carries no information: the error test it would face is passed by
construction.  Which spurious primes appear depends on the last digits of a
floating-point product of 384 transcendental factors, so it depends on the
PARI version, the working precision and the order of the product; the three
primes quoted in Sec. 6.7 come from one such run and are not a reproducible
invariant of the curve.  What is reproducible, and is the point, is that the
naive route reports small primes that the certified computation excludes.
